# Cursor Rules — Pardix Browser

## Project Context
Flutter mobile browser app (Android/iOS). Package: `com.dino.pardix`. Flutter SDK ^3.10.0.
Architecture: Clean Architecture + BLoC (flutter_bloc ^8.1.6).

## Layer Rules
- `lib/core/` — shared infrastructure, imported by all layers
- `lib/domain/` — pure Dart only, no Flutter/third-party imports
- `lib/data/` — implements domain contracts
- `lib/features/` — feature modules with their own bloc/ + widgets/ + services/
- `lib/presentation/` — top-level pages (HomePage, sheets)
- Dependency direction: presentation → features → domain ← data

## State Management
- ALL feature state goes in BLoC, never in widget setState
- BLoC events: NounVerbEvent (e.g., TabAddEvent, DownloadStartEvent)
- Use Equatable on all events and states
- Use Freezed for sealed state unions
- Access BLoC at the top level, pass callbacks to children — never context.read() deep in widget trees

## Code Style
- Files: snake_case.dart
- Classes: PascalCase
- Variables/methods: camelCase
- Private: _leadingUnderscore
- Constants: camelCase (not SCREAMING_SNAKE)
- Never hardcode colors → use AppColors (lib/core/resources/app_colors.dart)
- Never hardcode strings → use AppStrings (lib/core/resources/app_strings.dart)
- Never hardcode sizes → use AppSizes (lib/core/resources/app_size.dart)
- Never use print() → use AppLogger (lib/core/logger/logger.dart)

## Key Patterns
- Storage: always through StorageService (lib/data/services/storage_service.dart)
- HTTP: always through ApiClient (lib/core/api/api_client.dart)
- Media type detection: MediaUtils.detectType(url) → MediaType enum

## Logging — AppLogger (lib/core/logger/app_logger.dart)
Never use print() or the deprecated Logger class.

6 levels:
  AppLogger.verbose('Tag', 'trace')                        // dev only
  AppLogger.debug('Tag', 'debug info')                     // dev only
  AppLogger.info('Tag', 'event', params: {'k': 'v'})       // breadcrumb in release
  AppLogger.warning('Tag', 'issue', error: e)              // Crashlytics breadcrumb
  AppLogger.error('Tag', 'fail', error: e, stackTrace: s)  // Crashlytics non-fatal
  AppLogger.fatal('Tag', 'crash', error: e, stackTrace: s) // Crashlytics fatal

Firebase Analytics event (release only):
  AppLogger.event(AnalyticsEvent.tabOpened, params: {AnalyticsParam.isIncognito: false})

Tag = class/feature name: 'TabBloc', 'WebView', 'Download', 'Search', 'Storage'
Event/param constants always from analytics_event.dart — never hardcode strings

## Code Generation
- Files ending in .freezed.dart or .g.dart are generated — never edit manually
- After editing @freezed source: dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs

## Commands
- flutter analyze → must pass before any commit
- dart format lib/ → apply before any commit
- flutter test → run all tests
- dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs → after Freezed changes

## Critical Files
- lib/main.dart — entry point, Firebase init, deep links
- lib/presentation/pages/home/home_page.dart — main UI (1,248 lines, don't add to it)
- lib/features/webview/widgets/webview_page.dart — WebView + ad blocking + JS injection
- lib/features/tabs/bloc/tab_bloc.dart — master tab state

## Never Commit
- android/.key.properties
- android/app/*.jks
- android/app/google-services.json
- ios/Runner/GoogleService-Info.plist
- Any secrets or tokens

## Never Do
- Direct SharedPreferences calls — always use StorageService
- Create bare Dio/http.Client instances — use ApiClient
- Edit packages/flutter_inappwebview/ without explicit instruction
- Add more local state to home_page.dart — it's already at 1,248 lines
- Use print() — use AppLogger
- Use Logger.show() / Logger.error() — deprecated, use AppLogger
- Call FirebaseCrashlytics / FirebaseAnalytics directly — route through AppLogger
